    "html": "<article class=\"blog-post\">\n <header class=\"post-header\">\n <h1>Exploring the Basics of Responsive Design</h1>\n <div class=\"post-meta\">\n <span class=\"author\">By Alex Doe</span>\n <time datetime=\"2024-03-10\">March 10, 2024</time>\n </div>\n </header>\n <div class=\"post-content\">\n <p>Responsive design is a crucial aspect of modern web development. It ensures that your website looks great on devices of all sizes. In this article, we'll explore some fundamental concepts and techniques...</p>\n \n <h2>Why Responsive Design Matters</h2>\n <p>With the increasing variety of devices used to access the web, responsive design ensures a consistent user experience...</p>\n\n <h2>Key Techniques for Responsive Design</h2>\n <ul>\n <li><strong>Media Queries:</strong> Adjust styles based on device characteristics.</li>\n <li><strong>Flexible Grids:</strong> Use relative units to ensure elements resize automatically.</li>\n <li><strong>Fluid Images:</strong> Ensure images scale within their containers.</li>\n </ul>\n </div>\n <footer class=\"post-footer\">\n <section class=\"author-bio\">\n <h3>About the Author</h3>\n <p>Alex Doe is a seasoned web developer with a passion for creating intuitive and accessible web experiences...</p>\n </section>\n </footer>\n</article>",
